  "question": {
    "text": "The gravitational potential at a point above the surface of earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the acceleration due to gravity at that point is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume that the mean radius of earth to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6400</mn><mo> </mo><mi>km</mi></math>. The height of this point above the earth's surface is:",
    "image": null
  },
